      "message": "Chalard, thank you for the comment.\nFinally, we need to investigate the case you pointed out and additional UX after log in.\nAnd we need a time to conclude then, I want to abandon this patch and will re-open (or create newly) the patch after the conclusion.\n\nJust thought:\nfor mCaptivePortal.reportCaptivePortalDismissed() multiple times\n(This is not checked on our environment but..) I\u0027m not sure the case causes some problem (i.e. multiple internet tests to AP).\nBecause CaptivePortal.reportCaptivePortalDismissed() send APP_RETURN_DISMISSED to NetworkMonitor() but NetworkMonitor state is in ValidatedState in that case.\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/master/services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkMonitor.java#520\nIts state has no catch APP_RETURN_DISMISSED then problem might not be happened ?",
